  "interpretation": [
    "The old candidate admitted JSON false and 0.0 at verify_exit and produced MET signature/joint certificates with checker.valid=true; the independently implemented baseline signature helper rejected both. This is observed in the retained actual probe results.",
    "The new derived candidate requires exact int type and zero at the three process-exit checks. Actual four-case reports now agree with the fixed typed-exit contract.",
    "The semantic checker correctly checks a support claim conditional on the supplied explicit fact table. It does not authenticate the external adapter; the old false admission propagating to a valid semantic certificate illustrates this boundary rather than a demonstrated semantic-kernel error.",
    "The new fixtures were delivered to production helper functions in a declared derived scope. The frozen original CLI was not invoked and its fixed hash pin was not bypassed.",
    "The independent baseline function here is retained_signature, not a fresh invocation of its complete SQLite calibration. No equivalence of every adapter check is inferred."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This QA reads, hashes and statically compares existing artifacts. It does not repeat the four probes or the closed six-scenario calibration.",
    "Only verify_exit was dynamically varied. download_exit and gate gh_exit_code were statically confirmed to use the same strict helper and retained their integer-zero positive controls; no malformed-value probe at those two locations is claimed.",
    "The executed plan contains exactly 0, false, 0.0 and 1. Null, string zero and missing-key cases were discussed but not executed and are not counted as evidence.",
